{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner report on dap-grow after the input-work deploy (version 032f1c40 at 21:18). Archive passes now complete.\n\nMeasured at about 21:49 with a read token, against the 18:19 figures. Pass counts are the change in journal commit count, not observed passes:\n- Room A journal (sc_2dn76…): 1 commit to 37, so 36 passes. Tree bytes 745 to 8,698; blobs 6 to 111. That is about 221 tree bytes and about 2.9 blobs per pass.\n- Journal sc_nghnx…: 1 commit to 6, so 5 passes. Tree bytes 524 to 2,172, about 330 per pass.\n- The other three journals are unchanged at one commit.\n\nRoom A has now stalled at the tree-size limit, as 38be8e7c predicted. The tail from 21:23 to 21:48 has five diagnostics from the new version, from 21:31 to 21:43, all for the same pass: plan step, reason unavailable, parent read phase object-response, refusal too-large, type tree, ordinal 2, maximum 295. 8,698 is over the 8,487-byte allowance. No other refusal reason appears.\n\nPer ruling 6178a623 this stall is accepted, and nothing is lost: the entries stay in the room. fc2548ae is now the fix for Room A, and it is the builder's next item. At about 330 bytes per pass, journal sc_nghnx… reaches the limit after about 19 more passes if its backlog continues.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}